<title>MONACO: SWIMMING-MONACO INTERNATIONAL MEETING RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-MONACO INTERNATIONAL MEETING RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of finals on the second</p>
<p>day of the two-day Monaco international swimming meeting on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>Men's 400 metres individual medley</p>
<p>1. Marcel Wouda (Netherlands)   4 minutes 21.22 seconds</p>
<p>2. Xavier Marchand (France)     4:26.20</p>
<p>3. Mickey Halika (Israel)	 4:26.62</p>
<p>Men's 100 metres butterfly</p>
<p>1. Denis Silantiev (Ukraine)     53.41</p>
<p>2. Michael Klim (Australia)	53.57</p>
<p>3. Stefan Aartsen (Netherlands)  53.91</p>
<p>Men's 200 metres backstroke</p>
<p>1. Vladimir Selkov (Russia)	   2:01.58</p>
<p>2. Volodymir Nikolaychuk (Ukraine)  2:02.03</p>
<p>3. Ray Hass (Australia)		 2:04.25</p>
<p>Women's 400 metres freestyle</p>
<p>1. Kirsten Vlieghuis (Netherlands) 4:16.13</p>
<p>2. Solenne Figues (France)	   4:19.65</p>
<p>3. Hana Cerna (Czech Republic)     4:19.81</p>
<p>Women's 200 metres butterfly</p>
<p>1. Martina Moravcova (Slovakia)     2:13.03</p>
<p>2. Sophia Skou (Denmark)		2:15.04</p>
<p>3. Johanna Sjoberg (Sweden)	   2:15.96</p>
<p>Women's 100 metres backstroke</p>
<p>1. Olga Kochetkova (Russia)    1:02.80</p>
<p>2. Suze Valen (Netherlands)    1:03.82</p>
<p>3. Chen Yan (China)		1:04.13</p>
